notes:

SILENT COLONNADE -- two ambushes, and a dark-to-lit reveal that is the level.

  1 SPAWN (2,29) facing north in a light-0 shaft one cell wide. This is the
    darkest the game gets. There is exactly one direction.
  2 THE CLIMB: north, jog east, north again (x6, y11-23). Doglegs mean you
    never see more than four cells ahead. Three lit alcoves at (5,14), (7,18)
    and (5,21) are the only things to look at, and each one is a moment where
    the wall beside you steps in and out. Nothing lives here -- which is the
    point: the player starts expecting something.
  3 A door at (6,10) is the threshold. Beyond it --
  4 THE COLONNADE (x5-22 y3-9, light 2). Eighteen cells long, ten columns in
    two rows at y4 and y7, and the walking aisle is the two cells at y5-6,
    hard against the northern row. That adjacency is the whole trick: at one
    cell's range a column shows a tall bright face, and the next four recede
    behind it, which is the single most three-dimensional image this engine
    can produce. A husk shuffles at the far end (20,5): the only visible
    target, pulling you straight down the aisle. Landmark #1.
  5 AMBUSH ONE. The trigger is the aisle at (13,5)-(14,5), dead centre, where
    the bait has been leading you. Two sealed panels open at once, (12,2) and
    (13,2) in the north wall and (12,10)/(13,10) in the south, and four
    sleepers wake BEHIND and BESIDE you. The columns you have been walking
    past are now the only cover: that is why they were placed first.
  6 THE DOGLEG (x22 y10-12, east, then down to (25,14)). Cramped, light 1
    falling to 0. Just out of a fight and straight into a black corridor with
    no room to retreat. Deliberate.
  7 THE ARENA (x11-28 y15-27, light 6). The mouth at (25,15) is a light-0
    cell; one step later you are in an 18x13 hall at light 6, twenty metal
    columns on a 3-cell pitch and a glowing monolith at its centre. You enter
    beside a column, on the diagonal, so the reveal is depth, not a flat wall.
    The whole level exists to make that one step land.
  8 AMBUSH TWO fires immediately: the trigger at (24,16)/(25,16) is two cells
    inside the mouth, so reveal and trap are the same moment. Three sealed
    panels -- west (10,19), east (29,22), south (17,28) -- open on all sides.
    The AUTOGUN at (20,17) sits against the monolith: bait dropped in the
    dead centre of a crossfire.
  9 The column grid breaks the crossfire into a running fight instead of one
    firing line, and the monolith is the pivot: circle it and no two closets
    can see you at once.
 10 EXIT (x24-26 y29) in the arena's south-east, an alcove with a glow face,
    visible from the arena floor but NOT from the mouth -- so the last thing
    the level asks is that you cross it under fire.
end
